In early February, the launch of Altruist’s artificial intelligence tax planning tool sparked a selloff in wealth management stocks. But a new report by Fitch Ratings does not view the adoption of AI-enabled advisory tools as a near-term credit driver for the wealth management firms Fitch rates, including Charles Schwab, Raymond James, Ameriprise, Stifel and LPL Holdings.&nbsp;

